---
// TubuleRecessionDiagram.astro - High-contrast visual with 3D medical cross-section image showing exposed dentinal tubules, micro-leakage pathways, and acid nerve ignition
interface Props {
	class?: string;
}

const { class: className = '' } = Astro.props;
---

<div class={`tubule-diagram-wrapper ${className}`}>
	<div class="tubule-diagram-card">
		<div class="tubule-diagram-header">
			<h4 class="tubule-diagram-title">Mechanical Possible Root Causes</h4>
			<p class="tubule-diagram-desc">
				When gum tissue recedes, protective enamel ends, exposing the porous root surface (dentin). Over 30,000 microscopic fluid-filled tubules per square millimeter channel oral acids directly into the dental pulp and trigeminal nerve&nbsp;network.
			</p>
		</div>

		<!-- 3D Medical Cross-Section Image Container -->
		<div class="tubule-image-container">
			<img 
				src="/exposed-dentinal-tubules-cross-section.jpg" 
				alt="High-detail 3D anatomical cross-section of a human tooth showing gum recession, exposed dentinal tubules at the cervical root, and pulp nerve pathways connecting into the horizontal mandibular nerve canal (Trigeminal nerve CN V3)" 
				class="tubule-image"
				loading="lazy"
			/>
			
			<div class="tubule-pointer-callout">
				<div class="tubule-callout-arrow">
					<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
						<line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line>
						<polyline points="19 12 12 19 5 12"></polyline>
					</svg>
				</div>
				<p class="tubule-callout-text">
					<strong>Direct Trigeminal Connection (CN V3):</strong> The tooth pulp nerves exit the root apex directly into the horizontal Mandibular Nerve Canal. When gum recession exposes porous root dentin, dietary acids bypass enamel and trigger immediate nerve&nbsp;excitation.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- High-Magnification SEM Micrograph Container (Stacked: Photo on Top, Description Underneath) -->
		<div class="tubule-sem-container">
			<div class="tubule-sem-media">
				<img 
					src="/dentinal-tubules-sem-micrograph.jpg" 
					alt="Scanning electron micrograph (SEM) showing cross-section of exposed human dentinal tubules with open porous micro-channels under high magnification" 
					class="tubule-sem-image"
					loading="lazy"
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="tubule-sem-caption">
				<div class="tubule-sem-meta-row">
					<span class="tubule-sem-kicker">High-Resolution Electron Microscopy (SEM)</span>
					<span class="tubule-sem-source">Source: Ultrastructural Dental SEM Analysis (3,000x Mag)</span>
				</div>
				<h5 class="tubule-sem-title">The Microscopic Scale: 20,000 to 45,000 Tubules Per Square Millimeter</h5>
				<p class="tubule-sem-desc">
					Under electron microscopy, dentin is a dense matrix perforated with <strong>20,000 to 45,000 open fluid tubules per mm²</strong>. Even a minor 2 millimeter gum recession exposes <strong>50,000 to 90,000 open micro-tubule channels</strong> directly to the oral&nbsp;environment.
				</p>
				<p class="tubule-sem-desc" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
					<strong>The Acid Trigger Mechanism:</strong> Dietary and bacterial acids strip away the microscopic smear plugs that normally seal these pores. This causes rapid hydrodynamic fluid displacement and ionic acid penetration into the pulp, sending continuous pain signals through the apical foramen directly into the horizontal <strong>Mandibular Canal (Trigeminal CN V3)</strong>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.tubule-diagram-wrapper {
		margin: 3.5rem 0;
		width: 100%;
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	.tubule-diagram-card {
		background: radial-gradient(120% 120% at 50% 0%, #1e1136 0%, #0d081a 60%, #080410 100%);
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35);
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
		box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
		color: #e2e8f0;
	}

	.tubule-diagram-header {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		max-width: 780px;
		margin-left: auto;
		margin-right: auto;
	}

	.tubule-diagram-title {
		font-family: var(--font-heading, system-ui, sans-serif);
		font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.8vw, 1.95rem);
		font-weight: 900;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin: 0 0 0.85rem 0;
		line-height: 1.25;
		text-wrap: balance;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	.tubule-diagram-desc {
		font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.6vw, 1.05rem);
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: #cbd5e1;
		margin: 0;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.tubule-image-container {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 680px;
		margin: 0 auto 2.25rem auto;
		background: rgba(10, 6, 20, 0.6);
		border-radius: 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3);
		padding: 0.75rem;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		box-shadow: 0 15px 35px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.tubule-image {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		max-height: 560px;
		object-fit: contain;
		display: block;
		margin: 0 auto;
		border-radius: 0.85rem;
	}

	.tubule-pointer-callout {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12);
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35);
		border-radius: 0.85rem;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.tubule-callout-arrow {
		color: #c084fc;
		background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.25);
		border-radius: 50%;
		width: 38px;
		height: 38px;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		animation: bounceArrow 2s infinite ease-in-out;
	}

	@keyframes bounceArrow {
		0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
		50% { transform: translateY(4px); }
	}

	.tubule-callout-text {
		font-size: 0.92rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: #e2e8f0;
		margin: 0;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.tubule-callout-text strong {
		color: #fde047;
	}

	/* High-Magnification SEM Micrograph Section (Stacked: Image on Top, Description Underneath) */
	.tubule-sem-container {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 680px;
		margin: 0 auto 2.5rem auto;
		background: rgba(13, 8, 26, 0.7);
		border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.28);
		border-radius: 1.25rem;
		overflow: hidden;
		box-shadow: 0 15px 35px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}

	.tubule-sem-media {
		position: relative;
		width: 100%;
		max-height: 380px;
		background: #05020a;
		overflow: hidden;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.2);
	}

	.tubule-sem-image {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		max-height: 380px;
		object-fit: cover;
		display: block;
	}

	.tubule-sem-caption {
		padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}

	.tubule-sem-meta-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
	}

	.tubule-sem-kicker {
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #c084fc;
		letter-spacing: 0.03em;
		text-transform: none;
	}

	.tubule-sem-source {
		font-size: 0.76rem;
		font-style: italic;
		color: #94a3b8;
		letter-spacing: 0.01em;
	}

	.tubule-sem-title {
		font-family: var(--font-heading, system-ui, sans-serif);
		font-size: 1.18rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
		line-height: 1.35;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.tubule-sem-desc {
		font-size: 0.94rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: #cbd5e1;
		margin: 0;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.tubule-sem-desc strong {
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}
</style>
